Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ai-coding router mode: Codex controller and first
 live-run lessons

Add the Codex controller (danger-full-access session woken by router
relay; never run wait and relay together; recovery against router.db
and relay.log), open all external paths for OpenCode workers, have the
user trust a repo once at its root for Codex, and have the controller
prepare verification logs and requirement text for an offline Codex
reviewer. File isolation is no longer claimed as independence evidence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
